---
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";
---

<DocsLayout title="GitHub Actions">
  <h1>Deploying with GitHub Actions</h1>
  <p>
    The <a href="https://github.com/elloloop/identity"><code>elloloop/identity</code></a>
    repository ships a release workflow that builds and pushes a
    multi-arch container to GHCR on every <code>v*</code> tag. The
    workflow is reusable as a reference template.
  </p>

  <h2>Release workflow</h2>
  <p>
    File: <code>.github/workflows/release.yml</code>. Triggered by a Git
    tag matching <code>v*</code>. Pushes
    <code>ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:&lt;version&gt;</code> for both
    <code>linux/amd64</code> and <code>linux/arm64</code>.
  </p>
  <Code code={`name: Release
on:
  push:
    tags: ['v*']

env:
  REGISTRY: ghcr.io
  IMAGE_NAME: \${{ github.repository }}

jobs:
  build-and-push:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      contents: read
      packages: write
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - run: |
          VER="\${GITHUB_REF_NAME#v}"
          echo "$VER" > VERSION
      - uses: docker/setup-qemu-action@v3
      - uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@v3
      - uses: docker/login-action@v3
        with:
          registry: \${{ env.REGISTRY }}
          username: \${{ github.actor }}
          password: \${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
      - id: meta
        uses: docker/metadata-action@v5
        with:
          images: \${{ env.REGISTRY }}/\${{ env.IMAGE_NAME }}
          tags: |
            type=semver,pattern={{version}}
            type=semver,pattern={{major}}.{{minor}}
            type=semver,pattern={{major}}
            type=raw,value=latest,enable=\${{ !contains(github.ref, '-') }}
            type=sha,prefix=sha-
      - uses: docker/build-push-action@v5
        with:
          context: .
          platforms: linux/amd64,linux/arm64
          push: true
          target: server
          tags: \${{ steps.meta.outputs.tags }}
          labels: \${{ steps.meta.outputs.labels }}
          cache-from: type=gha
          cache-to: type=gha,mode=max
          sbom: true
          provenance: mode=max
          build-args: |
            VERSION=\${{ github.ref_name }}
            COMMIT=\${{ github.sha }}`} lang="yaml" title=".github/workflows/release.yml" />

  <h2>Cutting a release</h2>
  <Code code={`# Tag and push
git tag v0.1.0
git push origin v0.1.0

# The workflow produces these tags on GHCR:
#   ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:0.1.0
#   ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:0.1
#   ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:0
#   ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:latest      (non-prerelease only)
#   ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:sha-<commit>`} lang="bash" />

  <h2>Supply chain</h2>
  <p>The workflow asks Buildx for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>SBOM</strong> (<code>sbom: true</code>) — attached as an OCI artifact alongside the image.</li>
    <li><strong>Provenance</strong> (<code>provenance: mode=max</code>) — attestation for the SLSA build.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The runtime stage builds <code>FROM scratch</code> — the final image
    carries only the statically linked <code>identity</code> binary and the
    CA certificate bundle copied from the builder, with no base OS or
    package manager to track or patch.
  </p>

  <h2>Deploying the image</h2>
  <p>
    A typical CD pipeline pulls the image from GHCR and rolls it out via
    <code>kubectl set image</code>, Argo CD, or Flux. The exact wiring is
    out of scope for this repo, but
    <a href="/identity/docs/deployment/kubernetes">Kubernetes</a> covers
    a reference manifest.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
